      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chamberlain%2C_South_Dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city sits on the east bank of the Missouri River, where Lake Francis Case is dammed and I‑90 crosses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chamberlain%2C_South_Dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In Lakota, Chamberlain means “earth dwelling,” reflecting the area’s long indigenous presence.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chamberlain%2C_South_Dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Chamberlain serves as the county seat of Brule County, overseeing regional governance.",
